Palm's Email (com.palm.app.email 3.0.13600), as shipped on HP webOS 3.x.

Copyright Palm, Inc. / Hewlett-Packard. Never released under an open licence; distributed by
Lunacy as abandonware, like Mojo, the Prelude fonts and the TouchPad wallpapers: no owner has
asserted rights since webOS was discontinued.

Copied from the reference TouchPad, where it is pre-installed but lives in the user area of
the filesystem (/media/cryptofs/apps). The app is here as it was packaged, with Lunacy's changes
for a phone's card, codepoet's exception to rule 5 in CLAUDE.md (2026-10-08): HP laid Email out
for a TouchPad and left its phone layout unfinished. Each is marked [Lunacy] in its source:
in mail/source/MailApp.js, a tapped folder brings its messages over the folders and a tapped
message brings it over the list, a swipe in from the right edge brings the next panel over,
and the message panel's 448 px minimum applies only side by side; in
mail/source/MessageDisplay.js, the message view is no taller than its room, so it no longer
covers the toolbar and its grab handle. A tablet's layout is unchanged. The build scripts and specs that shipped beside it
(Rakefile, Gemfile, Gemfile.lock, ci_build.sh, build-ignore, jasminerunner.html, spec/) are
left out; nothing else is.
